#version 450
#extension GL_GOOGLE_include_directive : require
// MotionVersion::V3, build step E1 (gpu/V3.md section 3.5): the candidate-driven coarse-to-fine block search, both directions (z = 0: F01, 1: F10),
// one workgroup (64 threads) per block, dispatch gw_l x gh_l x 2 per level and iteration. Push: lvl = the level, iter = the iteration (0 / 1),
// mode bit 0 = hook (j) colour window (wired, a no-op: the wgt = 1 path); with -DV35=1 (v3_search_35, V3.5) mode bit 1 = the parent level's regularised records are in slot 0 (not 1). This is the pipeline of levels n-2 .. 0 (P_V3_SEARCH); the top level's
// exhaustive search is v3_search_top.comp (P_V3_SEARCH_TOP). The cost is section 2's (high-pass Y, Cb, Cr + the offset-corrected raw Y, 4 weights,
// mean over the window pixels whose target is inside the level; invalid below half). A "round" evaluates up to 16 candidates at once, 4 threads each
// (a quarter of the 64-pixel window per thread), the quarters summed through shared memory; the ring is a round of the 8 integer neighbours of the best.
// Candidate slots (iteration 0 of levels n-2 .. 1): 0 own parent x2, 1..3 the other nearest parents x2, 4 zero, 5 camera model, 6..9 dominant
// motions D0..D3, 10 reverse vector of the other direction, 11..15 unused; (iteration 1): 0 own iteration-0 result, 1..4 the 4 neighbours'
// iteration-0 results, 5 reverse vector of the other direction at the best's target, 6 zero, 7..9 D0..D2, 10 camera model. Slots with no
// candidate keep cflag 0 (cost 255); E2 fills 5..9 (iteration 0), 7..10 (iteration 1). cflag bit 0 = valid, bit 1 = no LAMBDA penalty.
// Level 0: candidates 0..4 = own parent x2 and the parents of the left / right / up / down neighbours x2, ring, then the fused Lucas-Kanade
// sub-pixel refinement (2 iterations). Output per block: vec4 (vx, vy, cost, amb) at BLK[l][dir][slot] (slot = iteration; level 0: 0).
// amb: level 0 copies it from its parent (the top level's second-best measure; E2 adds the level-1 probes).
#define V3S_TOP 0
#include "v3_search.glsl"
